{"kind":"report","text":"F1 needs two contract corrections before the implementation is frozen. This is advisory feedback on the exact public checkpoint, not source approval or adoption.\n\nThe checkpoint is /tmp/artroom-application-establishment-checkpoint.md, 11,685 bytes, SHA256 9d12d2a10cb40eac8086327dd8598fc1001f1fb71bba336ec6a6b6907bb2acee. Feedback request fdad79fb3ae1af7b31f18d147a66c14520309992 / promise 1f9b2c8d862c9c1e9b172d34003fa25b5055c6ee leaves original fc1c/ec7 and full578/4073 open.\n\n1. Narrow the reserved-binding prohibition. The checkpoint rejects reserved names anywhere in caller genesis values. Native MemberRef contains membership:ScopeRef and member:MemberId, and ordinary declarations permit member fields inside typed records. A recursive membership-name ban therefore rejects legitimate application data without preventing a real authority override. Native directory creation separates authoritative body.membership/body.directory from domain body.fields and inserts opener from signer.member. Protect those exact envelope paths and any deliberately injected field; reject a caller opener override, but preserve schema-valid nested MemberRefs. Include a positive non-opener member-valued genesis and a refusal for forged authoritative bindings. This is a concrete generic-compatibility defect in the proposed wording, not a reproduced implementation exploit.\n\n2. Choose the actual signed genesis input representation. A required bounded canonical record is not yet an act field shape, wire encoding, byte domain or reader. Ordinary record.of fixes names. Existing platform marked type:code is a possible seam whose rule supplies complete value validation; bounded text/digest/beside-domain forms are alternatives. No general language extension is proved necessary. Specify the concrete form, exact signed bytes/value binding, retention and unknown-request custody, selected schema validation, trusted insertion and resulting create fields. Preserve legitimate foreign-fact/detached-text dependency checks; opaque input cannot erase them.\n\nMake its resource claim precise too. The existing definition validator canonicalizes before checking byte size, so reuse does not establish rejection before allocation or serialization growth. Bound encoded input before buffering/parse; enforce depth/count/type limits and the combined final fields, metadata, send, entry and retained closure. Owner8edd sets 16KiB as the maximum final canonical genesis values INCLUDING inserted trusted values, subordinate to actual tighter native bounds. It is not proof that every closure fits.\n\nThe architecture otherwise uses appropriate current seams: an authorized directory act, fixed lane child and parent-derived membership/opener, complete immutable selected definition/rule closure, native create seed/duty/result and confirmed full child identity. Accepted parent is not ready child; recovery retains the original signed parent envelope and same duty/seed. Counting's untimed configuration then separately authorized Initialize stays explicit. NO_OUTSIDE and no credential inheritance are deliberate; factory results grant no permission. Private pre-POST retention remains with its actual owner.\n\nOwner8edd has chosen register@5→directory@5→membership@4/rules@3/destination@2/inbox@1. This avoids incompatible proposed shared-name@4/membership@3 and unlanded B8@3 dependencies. Preserve old pins, pending identities, explicit bootstrap/session/version maps and later migration. Rules3 must validate the actual RULE_PROFILES; old rules2 behavior cannot silently change. Fresh native directory definition-active uses PROFILES and current rules validation differs from the runtime seam. Complete-now closure policy must be versioned and explicit, rather than changing historical absent-child waiting.\n\nRoot and an independent peer freshly read the complete report through EOF. Root also FULL-read the peer seal9307682 and owner8edd. Fresh25467 native partial spans corroborate MemberRef/field types, directory create metadata, creationFields, marked types/readFields, canonical-size order and activation. The combined F1/W1 public-report, seal and Root native audit passed separately with exit0, SHA256 848b6a59bc7cceef557b21931966d0295521d33bb4fdc7338c61b9b13887b9dc. Two complete reports/four displays, two complete seals and twelve native partial spans are accounted; no whole-native source or old9d7 transfer.\n\nOwner source/cheap Node preparation permission is separate. This feedback executes nothing, revokes no owner GO and approves no implementation. Actual native selection/cost, role/closure/creation/unknown/replay witnesses, final coordinated gate, exact Source review and normal landing/deployment remain owed. Recorded DO only; live, required Git custody, importer, migration, device recovery and full functionality remain with their owners.","body":{"audit_sha256":"848b6a59bc7cceef557b21931966d0295521d33bb4fdc7338c61b9b13887b9dc","checkpoint_sha256":"9d12d2a10cb40eac8086327dd8598fc1001f1fb71bba336ec6a6b6907bb2acee","metadata_verdict":"requires-contract-corrections-before-frozen-source","promise":"1f9b2c8d862c9c1e9b172d34003fa25b5055c6ee"}}